  body: |
    # Notional income in the ESA source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source calls income not received but treated as held notional income and lists several potential bases, with normal assessment rules and any appropriate disregard.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 51456–51462 distinguish actual income, possible notional bases, liable-relative payments and service-user exceptions. A missing payment does not establish notional income or fraud. Historical programme wording is not a current duration rule.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 51456, PDF page 127](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=127)
    - [DMG 51457, PDF page 127](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=127)
    - [DMG 51458, PDF page 127](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=127)
    - [DMG 51459, PDF page 128](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=128)
    - [DMG 51461, PDF page 128](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=128)
    - [DMG 51462, PDF page 128](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=128)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

